# We use pnpm workspaces — npm/yarn lockfiles shouldn't land here
package-lock.json
yarn.lock

# `actions/setup-node` with `registry-url:` writes a registry auth token into
# .npmrc on the runner, so a working tree mid-CI holds a real credential. Nothing
# here is meant to be committed — ignore it so a stray `git add .` in a future
# change can't publish one. (The repo publishes via OIDC trusted publishing and
# needs no committed token.)
.npmrc
